NAME
       hsh - A simple UNIX command interpreter

SYNOPSIS
       ./hsh

DESCRIPTION
       hsh is a command language interpreter that executes commands read from the 
       standard input or from a file. It mimics the basic functionality of 
       the standard UNIX shell.

       When hsh is running, it displays a prompt and waits for the user to type 
       a command.

ENVIRONMENT
       The shell uses the PATH environment variable to locate executable files.

EXIT STATUS
       hsh returns the exit status of the last command executed.

